test_polynomial`"},"168":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-166","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#test-suites","content":"20"},"169":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-167","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#test-suites","content":"18"},"170":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-168","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#test-suites","content":"Random"},"171":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-169","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#test-suites","content":"`numpy.random.tests.test_random`"},"172":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-170","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#test-suites","content":"0 (module skipped)"},"173":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-171","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#test-suites","content":"—"},"174":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-172","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#test-suites","content":"**Total**"},"175":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-173","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#test-suites","content":"**5,275**"},"176":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-174","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#test-suites","content":"**329**"},"177":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-175","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#test-suites","content":"Three suites fail to *import* rather than run any of their own tests, and are counted as\nfully skipped: `test_numeric` builds a non-numeric-dtype array at module import time, which\nthe dtype ban refuses; `test_linalg` and `test_random` each mutate an array at\nmodule import time, which flopscope's immutable arrays refuse. Each of these collection\nfailures is caught and reported as a single module-level skip rather than failing the\nrun — see `pytest_make_collect_report` in `tests/numpy_compat/conftest.py`."},"178":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-176","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#test-suites","content":"All other failures are tracked as xfails in `tests/numpy_compat/xfails.py`."},"179":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-177","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#running-the-tests","content":"Tests use `pytest-xdist` for parallel execution across all CPU cores."},"180":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-178","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#running-the-tests","content":"The numpy\\_compat tests are excluded from the default `pytest` run (via `pyproject.toml` `addopts`) to prevent the monkeypatch from contaminating the main test suite. They run as a separate step in CI."},"181":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-179","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"Tests that fail due to known, accepted differences are tracked in `tests/numpy_compat/xfails.py`. Each entry maps a test pattern to a categorized reason. As measured on numpy 2.2.6:"},"182":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-180","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"Category"},"183":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-181","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"Count"},"184":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-182","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"Meaning"},"185":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-183","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"`SUBCLASS_RETURN`"},"186":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-184","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"26"},"187":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-185","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"A patched op returns/propagates `FlopscopeArray` where the test expects a plain `ndarray` or scalar"},"188":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-186","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"`NONNUMERIC_DTYPE_BANNED`"},"189":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-187","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"21"},"190":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-188","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"The dtype ban (a numeric allowlist: bool, integer, float, complex) refuses a non-numeric-dtype array — object, string, bytes, structured/void, datetime64, or timedelta64 — the test constructs or requires directly"},"191":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-189","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"`NEEDS_TRIAGE`"},"192":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-190","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"16"},"193":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-191","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"Passes in isolation but fails under the parametrize sweep — order-dependent state pollution, not yet root-caused"},"194":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-192","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"`NOT_IMPLEMENTED`"},"195":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-193","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"11"},"196":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-194","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"Function exists but lacks a kwarg or edge case (missing `out=`, `where=`, `subok=`, …)"},"197":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-195","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"`NUMPY_INTERNAL`"},"198":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-196","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"1"},"199":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-197","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"Test uses numpy internals (`_umath_tests`, internal type tables)"},"200":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-198","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"`UPSTREAM_NUMPY_FLAKE`"},"201":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-199","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"1"},"202":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-200","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"A numpy-side tolerance/precision flake unrelated to flopscope"},"203":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-201","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"`BY_DESIGN`"},"204":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-202","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"1"},"205":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-203","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"flopscope intentionally diverges from numpy's behavior here"},"206":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-204","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"immutability"},"207":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-205","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"1"},"208":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-206","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"flopscope arrays are immutable; the test mutates one in place"},"209":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-207","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#known-divergences-xfails","content":"`test_numeric`, `test_linalg`, and `test_random` no longer contribute xfails to this table at\nall — all three suites fail to *import* on this numpy version (see Test\nsuites above), so none of their individual tests are collected."},"210":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-208","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#triaging-new-failures","content":"Run a suite: `uv run pytest tests/numpy_compat/ --pyargs <module> -n auto --tb=line`"},"211":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-209","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#triaging-new-failures","content":"Categorize each failure"},"212":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-210","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#triaging-new-failures","content":"If it's a bug we should fix, create an issue"},"213":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-211","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#triaging-new-failures","content":"If it's an accepted divergence, add it to `xfails.py`"},"214":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-212","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#why-monkeypatching-not-subclassing","content":"We considered alternatives:"},"215":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-213","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#why-monkeypatching-not-subclassing","content":"**Array subclass with `__array_ufunc__`**: Would intercept ufunc calls, but flopscope arrays are plain `numpy.ndarray` by design -- no custom tensor class."},"216":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-214","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#why-monkeypatching-not-subclassing","content":"**Running tests with `import flopscope as np`**: NumPy's test files import from `numpy._core`, `numpy.testing`, etc. -- can't redirect all internal imports."},"217":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-215","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#why-monkeypatching-not-subclassing","content":"**Monkeypatching with frozen numpy**: Simple, works with NumPy's existing test infrastructure, tests exactly what users experience (same function signatures), and the frozen-numpy trick prevents infinite recursion."},"218":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-216","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#related-pages","content":"Running with Docker — containerized client-server setup"},"219":{"id":"/docs/development/contributing-217","page_id":"/docs/development/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/development/contributing#related-pages","content":"Client-Server Model — architecture overview"},"220":{"id":"/docs/development/release","page_id":"/docs/development/release","type":"page","content":"Release Process","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/release"},"221":{"id":"/docs/development/release-0","page_id":"/docs/development/release","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/release#version-bumps","content":"Version bumps"},"222":{"id":"/docs/development/release-1","page_id":"/docs/development/release","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/release#end-to-end-flow","content":"End-to-end flow"},"223":{"id":"/docs/development/release-2","page_id":"/docs/development/release","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/release#multi-package-lockstep","content":"Multi-package lockstep"},"224":{"id":"/docs/development/release-3","page_id":"/docs/development/release","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/development/r