dot` bill this flat `4` as well. The\nexceptions are the ops that mirror a bare `fnp.*` twin and take *its* complex factor\ninstead of this dense rule: `linalg.outer` bills factor 6 like `outer`; `linalg.matmul`,\n`linalg.tensordot`, and `linalg.vecdot` bill the same **exact** per-call contraction\nfactor as `matmul`/`tensordot`/`vecdot`; `linalg.trace` bills 2 like `trace` (a diagonal\nsum, not a factorization); and `linalg.cross` bills 4.7 like `cross`. (Where such a row\nstill carries `complex_factor = 4.0` in the registry it is inert metadata — the\ndelegation or the op-specific factor applies instead.)"},"1862":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-614","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#linalg-direct-non-iterative","content":"Op"},"1863":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-615","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#linalg-direct-non-iterative","content":"flop\\_cost (per matrix)"},"1864":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-616","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#linalg-direct-non-iterative","content":"basis"},"1865":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-617","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#linalg-direct-non-iterative","content":"source"},"1866":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-618","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#linalg-direct-non-iterative","content":"`linalg.cholesky`"},"1867":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-619","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#linalg-direct-non-iter