eturns something smaller cannot buy a cheaper scan; the returned index arrays are not charged"},"2537":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1289","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather-ops-with-distinct-charged-siblings","content":"`_array_ops.py`"},"2538":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1290","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather-ops-with-distinct-charged-siblings","content":"`getitem` (`arr[key]`)"},"2539":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1291","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather-ops-with-distinct-charged-siblings","content":"basic indexing (int/slice/newaxis/Ellipsis, or a tuple thereof): `0` (view); advanced (fancy/boolean) indexing: `4·numel(output)` + `numel(mask)` per boolean-mask part (weight 1.0)"},"2540":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1292","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather-ops-with-distinct-charged-siblings","content":"DECLARED: fancy gather billed at the `take` rate; boolean-mask parts additionally scan like `compress`"},"2541":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1293","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather-ops-with-distinct-charged-siblings","content":"`_ndarray.py`"},"2542":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1294","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather-ops-with-distinct-charged-siblings","content":"`getitem` is the one op in this table with no module-level `fnp.<name>` call form — it\nbills `FlopscopeArray.__getitem__`, i.e. `arr[key]` syntax, not a function call. See\nthe unifying philosophy for\nthe basic-vs-advanced-indexing distinction this formula rests on."},"2543":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1295","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather-ops-with-distinct-charged-siblings","content":"`mask_indices` prices only the mask that `mask_func` produces, not the index arrays it\nreturns, so — unlike the dtype-neutral index generators below —\nits charge scales with the mask's dtype. The charge is also floored at n² (int dtype):\n`mask_func` receives numpy's internal `ones((n, n), int)` probe as an argument, so it\ncan capture that reference and return an arbitrarily small result while still having\nhad the full probe handed to it. `triu_indices`/`tril_indices` are separate ops with\ntheir own dtype-neutral formula and are unaffected by this."},"2544":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1296","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#index-generators","content":"These ops return coordinate/index arrays rather than values, and price\n**dtype-neutrally** — the billed count is `numel` of the returned index array(s)\nregardless of the array's actual integer dtype, since the work (computing positions)\ndoes not depend on how wide the position values happen to be stored:"},"2545":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1297","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#index-generators","content":"Op"},"2546":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1298","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#index-generators","content":"flop\\_cost"},"2547":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1299","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#index-generators","content":"basis"},"2548":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1300","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#index-generators","content":"`unravel_index`"},"2549":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1301","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#index-generators","content":"`numel` of the returned index arrays"},"2550":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1302","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#index-generators","content":"DECLARED"},"2551":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1303","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#index-generators","content":"`ravel_multi_index`"},"2552":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1304","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#index-generators","content":"`numel(output)` (= `N`, the number of index tuples)"},"2553":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1305","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#index-generators","content":"DECLARED"},"2554":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1306","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#index-generators","content":"`diag_indices`, `diag_indices_from`"},"2555":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1307","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","ur