ries — at \\~2 FLOPs each, so at `edge_order=1` the cost is independent of axis length). Any other accepted `edge_order` (0, 2, or a non-integer in (1, 2]; > 2 is rejected) runs the 5-FLOP second-order boundary stencil on each of the two boundary hyperplanes instead of the 2-FLOP one-sided difference, adding `+6·S/L` per selected axis (`L = f.shape[axis]`). Each coord-array axis adds a spacing surcharge (uniform: `+3(L−1)`; non-uniform: `+3S(L−2)/L + 10(L−2) + 3(L−1) + 4S/L`)"],[2539,"basic indexing (int/slice/newaxis/Ellipsis, or a tuple thereof): `0` (view); advanced (fancy/boolean) indexing: `4·numel(output)` + `numel(mask)` per boolean-mask part (weight 1.0)"],[752,"Basic usage"],[1667,"basis"],[1766,"basis"],[1777,"basis"],[1820,"basis"],[1864,"basis"],[1959,"basis"],[2001,"basis"],[2034,"basis"],[2086,"basis"],[2183,"basis"],[2256,"basis"],[2284,"basis"],[2331,"basis"],[2355,"basis"],[2418,"basis"],[2441,"basis"],[2467,"basis"],[2520,"basis"],[2547,"basis"],[2598,"basis"],[1212,"Before group intersection, any axis stretched from size `1` to a larger output\nsize is removed from the carried candidate group. So singleton broadcasting by\nitself does not preserve symmetry. In this example, though, `plain_tensor`\nalready carries the same analytically provable `S_2` symmetry on `(0, 1)`, so\n`broadcast_sum` keeps that shared block."],[483,"Before its first entry, `summary_dict()` returns the canonical empty mapping."],[261,"Before tagging, `check-sync-versions` asserts that all eight version\nlocations agree. Run locally:"],[269,"Before the first release will succeed, configure two things outside the\nrepo. The Trusted Publisher steps must be repeated for **each** PyPI\nproject name being published."],[2733,"Bespoke cost formula"],[1612,"billed FLOP/s saved"],[1537,"Billed FLOPs for an `N = 100` elementwise call under production rates (`multiply`: weight\n1, factor 6; `add`: weight 1, factor 2; `sin`: weight 16, factor 3.4):"],[1567,"Billing follows the loop numpy